public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }

    // 3^31 is the largest power of 3 that fits within the range of int (-2^31 to 2^31 - 1)
    // so we check if n is a power of 3 by taking the logarithm base 3 and rounding down
    double log3 = Math.log10(n) / Math.log10(3);
    return (log3 == (int) log3);
}
```

This solution uses the fact that `log3 = x` if and only if `3^x = n`. By taking the logarithm base 3 of `n` and rounding down to an integer, we can check if `n` is a power of 3 without loops or recursion.

Note that this solution assumes the `Math.log10` and `Math.log10(3)` methods, which are part of the standard Java library. If you need to use a different library or implement these methods yourself, you may need to adjust the code accordingly.

